    "explanation": "To both parties: this is a SGD 4.50 no-show cancellation fee charged to the rider on trip TRP-02732 and still live on EV-FARE-02732 (cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). A no-show fee stands only if POL-NS-01 is satisfied in all four limbs; the rider wins by breaking any one.\n\nI accept limbs (a), (b) and (d). EV-TRIP-02732 carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 17:06:36 (a); the trace places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 17:06:36, with 22 qualifying in-geofence fixes and min_distance_m 0.157, which is the POL-NS-02 test (b); and the trip terminated by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW at 17:13:20 with no boarding event (d). The fare ledger reconciles (4.50 = platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.50), so the figure in dispute is the correct net amount.\n\nThe case turns on limb (c), the continuous in-geofence dwell of at least the free waiting period in force - 180 s, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec; the 300 s STANDARD minimum_dwell_sec applies only to pre-version-2 records and not to this one. The dwell is measured from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the driver's 'arrived' tap (POL-NS-01(c)); the tap here is BUTTON, so POL-NS-12's platform-confirmed (GPS_AUTO) treatment does not apply, and trip_record.wait_time_min 6.7 is only the tap-to-cancellation interval, not an in-geofence dwell measurement.\n\nThe only evidence for that dwell is EV-GPS-02732, and it is impaired. Its admissibility weight is 0.39, with issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE. Its own derived figures conflict: longest_qualifying_run reports 400 s (17:06:36-17:13:16, 22 fixes), but the underlying run list is 60 s (17:06:36-17:07:36) and 145 s (17:10:51-17:13:16), with longest_run_sec 145 and a stated shortfall of 35 s. The 400 s figure spans a 195 s sampling hole from 17:07:36 to 17:10:51 inside the waiting window, and a gap longer than 120 s inside the waiting window makes the trace impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08(b).\n\nAgainst the driver: the 400 s dwell is rejected. It counts the unobserved 195 s as presence. The only route to join the 60 s and 145 s intervals is POL-NS-06(i), which requires a present and populated traffic advisory of a qualifying type; EV-ADVIS-02732-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0), so limb (i) is unavailable, the intervals may not be summed, and the trace's own excursion block records the stretch as unmeasurable. Without it, no observed continuous run reaches 180 s, and the driver's 3.60 payout under POL-NS-07 (80% of 4.50) cannot be fixed.\n\nAgainst the rider: the full refund is not supported either. The trace does not show the driver leaving the geofence; it simply fails to observe him for 195 s. The limb therefore cannot be affirmed, and because the gap is unobserved it cannot be denied either - limb (c) is UNDECIDED over the impaired stretch, and an undecided limb supports neither the fee nor the refund.\n\nThe rider's other routes do not help. POL-NS-04 cannot run (EV-CHAT-02732 carries 0 messages; no in-app calls), and the absent rider track makes its limb (c) undecidable; under POL-NS-11 that is neutral, does not exonerate the rider and does not impair the driver's arrival and dwell evidence. POL-NS-05 is not engaged - at the 'arrived' timestamp the driver was at the pin, not more than 300 m away and not at 15 km/h or more - so no false-arrival referral arises. POL-NS-03 does not apply: the stationary fixes are inside the arrival radius, not outside it.\n\nThe case therefore escalates. The sole evidence for the deciding fact - the continuous in-geofence dwell - is impaired under POL-NS-08(b), which engages POL-NS-09(e); and confidence, capped by that sole carrier at 0.39, is below the 0.70 floor, engaging POL-NS-09(a). Escalation is terminal: no monetary ruling issues, and the SGD 4.50 fee is HELD rather than collected or refunded while review is pending. POL-GEN-05 is not reached because the monetary effect is nil.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: on the full-resolution telemetry, did the driver hold position inside the 50 m geofence continuously for at least the 180 s free waiting period before cancelling at 17:13:20 - the answer turning on the 195 s hole from 17:07:36 to 17:10:51? The reviewer may request a full-resolution GPS export as record-type evidence under POL-GEN-04(b). The escalation packet carries both advocate briefs, the pre-pass report, the clauses relied on (POL-NS-01, POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05, POL-NS-06, POL-NS-07, POL-NS-08, POL-NS-09, POL-NS-11, POL-GEN-02) and this reasoning. No clause-mandated referral fires on these facts (the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip: no_show_terminations_30d 1, below 4, and 1/81 well under 0.08)."
