    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 4.50 no-show fee on trip TRP-02732 is placed on hold and the case goes to a human reviewer. The fee turns on one question — did the driver hold position inside the pickup geofence continuously for the 180-second free waiting period in force (EV-TRIP-02732 platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180 s) before cancelling at 17:13:20 under RIDER_NO_SHOW? Limbs (a), (b) and (d) of POL-NS-01 are on the record: the driver-arrived event at 17:06:36, 22 qualifying in-radius fixes on EV-GPS-02732 (STANDARD arrival radius 50 m), and the driver's RIDER_NO_SHOW termination, which is one of the three codes POL-NS-01(d) recognises. Limb (c) cannot be decided. The only measurement of in-geofence dwell is EV-GPS-02732, and that trace is impaired at weight 0.39 with issue codes GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW and LOW_COVERAGE: it carries a 195-second sampling hole from 17:07:36 to 17:10:51 — longer than the 120-second threshold that makes a trace defective under POL-NS-08(b) — and reports only 80.5% coverage. Outside the hole the admitted readings show a longest continuous in-geofence run of 145 seconds (17:10:51-17:13:16), with a 60-second run before the hole; the derived 400-second 'longest_qualifying_run' spans the hole and so cannot show continuity across it. The only route to 180 continuous seconds runs through the unmeasured stretch, so the limb is undecided: it is not affirmatively met, so the driver's claim to a 400-second dwell is not established; and a 35-second shortfall is not affirmatively proved either, so the rider's POL-NS-06 refund is not established. The accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) cannot help either side because EV-ADVIS-02732-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0). Because the sole evidence for this deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08, the ruling may not exceed PARTIAL_REFUND and escalates under POL-NS-09; and the POL-GEN-02(2) cap on confidence is the trace's 0.39, below the 0.70 floor, which also escalates under POL-NS-09(a). No monetary outcome issues and the SGD 4.50 stays on hold, neither collected nor refunded. On the parties' claims: the driver's limbs (a), (b) and (d) points are accepted, the arrival marker was not false so POL-NS-05 is not engaged, POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider (EV-CHAT-02732 carries 0 messages and no in-app calls), and the fare ledger is clean with no POL-NS-08(d) defect (its SGD 4.50 line reconciles with platform_policy) — but the 400-second dwell claim is rejected for the reason above, so POL-NS-07 cannot fix the SGD 3.60 payout and the DRIVER_COMPENSATION outcome is not available; the driver's statement that he 'waited the full time' is his own assertion, carries no weight multiplier and names no clause test, so it neither lifts the confidence cap nor carries the dwell. The rider's points that the period is 180 s and not 300, that dwell must be read on the GPS clock rather than the 17:06:36 arrival tap (arrival_marker is BUTTON, so POL-NS-12 does not apply), and that the 400-second figure cannot bridge the hole are accepted — but the 35-second shortfall and the consequent full refund under POL-NS-06 rest on the same impaired trace and are not affirmatively established, so no refund issues. The open question for the reviewer is whether the driver remained at the pin through the 17:07:36-17:10:51 hole; a full-resolution GPS export covering that window would settle it."
